  <ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="f50" contextRef="c1">&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;calibri&#39;;font-size: 10pt;line-height: 107.9%;margin-bottom: 8pt;margin-top: 0;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;calibri&#39;;font-size: 10pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;1.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;calibri&#39;;font-size: 10pt;line-height: 107.9%;margin-bottom: 8pt;margin-top: 0;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;calibri&#39;;font-size: 10pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;A. Prior Period Adjustment&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;calibri&#39;;font-size: 10pt;line-height: 107.9%;margin-bottom: 8pt;margin-top: 0;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;calibri&#39;;font-size: 10pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;During the second quarter of 2026, the Company identified an error originating in 2023 that resulted in an overstatement of certain asset balances. The correction reduced Miscellaneous Other Assets (Account 43) by $284,602 and Oil Inventory (Account 16) by $57,502, with a corresponding $342,104 reduction in Prior Period Adjustments to Beginning Retained Income (Account 705). The adjustment was noncash and had no effect in operating, investing, or financing activities during the 2026 reporting period.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;calibri&#39;;font-size: 10pt;line-height: 107.9%;margin-bottom: 8pt;margin-top: 0;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;calibri&#39;;font-size: 10pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;B. Balance Sheet Schedule110 - Account 67 Asset Retirement Obligations&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;calibri&#39;;font-size: 10pt;line-height: 107.9%;margin-bottom: 8pt;margin-top: 0;"&gt;&lt;div  style="font-family: &#39;calibri&#39;;font-size: 10pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;The asset retirement obligation is reflected at the fair value of estimated future costs, which are expected to be incurred during continuing operations and at the end of Arrowhead Offshore Pipeline&amp;#8217;s life. &lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;calibri&#39;;font-size: 10pt;line-height: 107.9%;margin-bottom: 8pt;margin-top: 0;"&gt;&lt;div  style="font-size: 10pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;table style="border: none;border-collapse: collapse;margin-bottom: .001pt;width: 4.47in;"&gt;&lt;tr style="height: 0.20in;"&gt;&lt;td style="background: #dce6f1;border-bottom: solid #ffffff 1.0pt;border-left-style: none;border-right: solid #ffffff 1.0pt;border-top: solid #ffffff 1.0pt;padding-bottom: 0;padding-left: 5.4pt;padding-right: 5.4pt;padding-top: 0;vertical-align: bottom;width: 126.1pt;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;calibri&#39;;font-size: 10pt;line-height: 107.9%;margin-bottom: 8pt;margin-top: 0;"&gt;&lt;div  style="font-size: 10pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="background: #dce6f1;border-bottom: solid #ffffff 1.0pt;border-left: solid #ffffff 1.0pt;border-right: solid #ffffff 1.0pt;border-top: solid #ffffff 1.0pt;padding-bottom: 0;padding-left: 5.4pt;padding-right: 5.4pt;padding-top: 0;vertical-align: bottom;width: 17.15pt;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;calibri&#39;;font-size: 10pt;line-height: 107.9%;margin-bottom: 8pt;margin-top: 0;"&gt;&lt;div  style="font-size: 10pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="background: #dce6f1;border-bottom: solid #ffffff 1.0pt;border-left: solid #ffffff 1.0pt;border-right: solid #ffffff 1.0pt;border-top: solid #ffffff 1.0pt;padding-bottom: 0;padding-left: 5.4pt;padding-right: 5.4pt;padding-top: 0;vertical-align: top;width: 93.6pt;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 8pt;line-height: 107.9%;margin-bottom: 8pt;margin-top: 0;text-align: right;"&gt;&lt;div style="color: #000000;font-family: &